"""Build mode constraint: `debug` vs `release`.

`buckshot//mode:mode[release]` on a target platform's configuration opts
that whole build into optimized output; anything without an explicit mode
value behaves as `debug` (the constraint default), so selects only ever
need a `release` arm plus `DEFAULT`.

The toolchains consume this directly — no per-rule flags needed:

- rust (`downloaded_rust_toolchain rustc_flags`): release adds
  `-Copt-level=3 -Cdebug-assertions=off -Coverflow-checks=off`
  (cargo's release profile, minus codegen-units/LTO tuning which match
  rustc's own defaults anyway). Applies to every rustc invocation in the
  target configuration, first- and third-party crates alike.
- c++ (`zig_cxx_toolchain c/cxx_compiler_flags`): release adds
  `-O3 -DNDEBUG`.

Host/exec-configuration compilation (proc macros, build scripts, build
tools) never sees a mode value, so it always builds unoptimized —
slower to compile, identical output.
"""

constraint(
    name = "mode",
    default = "debug",
    values = ["debug", "release"],
    visibility = ["PUBLIC"],
)
